    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file `extract_json.py` that calls a hosted LLM to extract structured JSON from text, I need to choose a concrete external provider. I will use Amazon Bedrock, which is a service that provides access to various foundation models, including those for natural language processing tasks like extracting structured data from text. I will import the necessary SDK and use a specific model identifier to make the provider identifiable in the code. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789855306953,
          "start": 1789855303581
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bbb0879d00122bQs2vgfhF6MX",
      "message_id": "msg_0bbb08217001V076RWbGQJDkj2",
      "session_id": "ses_f444f7e0effeZbYXcIWbBza7yR",
